-- examples/checks/agg-life-demo-check.rofl — agg_life_demo, THE BOARD ACROSS
-- TICKS, THE NEIGHBOUR COUNT AS A CELL (examples/life/README.md). The rules
-- are examples/life/life.rofl, run 8 ticks deep with --explain, so the last
-- tick is evaluated: a glider from the top left and a blinker at the bottom
-- right on a 10 by 10 board. Every tick checks itself against an oracle
-- written by a script that plays the game apart from these rules (a plain
-- JavaScript loop over a set of cells): the live cells, the population,
-- how many cells have 0 to 8 live neighbours, the count of every cell at
-- ticks 0 and 3, and the cause cone of the glider's head at tick 8. A
-- disagreement is a row of lf_wrong, carried to the last tick so that an
-- earlier one is not lost with its tick.
--
-- BY HAND: the glider (1,0) (2,1) (0,2) (1,2) (2,2) is back in the same
-- shape, two cells down and two to the right, at tick 8: (3,2) (4,3) (2,4)
-- (3,4) (4,4). The blinker lies down (6,8) (7,8) (8,8) at the even ticks and
-- stands (7,7) (7,8) (7,9) at the odd. The population is 8 at every tick,
-- and the blinker is no cause of the glider's head.
